ographer, book reviewer, ecological consultant, and lecturer.[1][2][3][4]"], "37": [37, "link", "short stories", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Collected_Stories_of_Frank_Herbert", "Franklin Patrick Herbert Jr. (October 8, 1920 – February 11, 1986) was an American science-fiction author, best known for his 1965 novel Dune and its five sequels. He also wrote short stories and worked as a newspaper journalist, photographer, book reviewer, ecological consultant, and lecturer.[1][2][3][4]"], "38": [38, "link", "[ 1 ]", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "#cite_note-1", "[1]"], "39": [39, "link", "[ 2 ]", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "#cite_note-2", "[2]"], "40": [40, "link", "[ 3 ]", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "#cite_note-3", "[3]"], "41": [41, "link", "[ 4 ]", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "#cite_note-4", "[4]"], "42": [42, "link", "[ 5 ]", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "#cite_note-RIF-5", "[5]"], "43": [43, "link", "genre", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genre", "Dune is one of the best-selling science fiction novels of all time,[5] and the series is a classic of the science-fiction genre.[6] The series has been adapted numerous times, including the feature film David Lynch's Dune (1984), the miniseries Frank Herbert's Dune (2000) and Children of Dune (2003), and a motion picture trilogy currently in production, with Denis Villeneuve's Dune (2021) and Dune: Part Two (2024) having been released with Dune: Part Three (2026) being the last installment.[7][8]"], "44": [44, "link", "[ 6 ]", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "#cite_note-Kunzru2015-6", "[6]"], "45": [45, "link", "David Lynch", null, null, null, null, false, null, null, null, null, "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Lynch", "Dune is one of the best-sell